# PART 1 — PRODUCT REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT (PRD)

---

## 1.1 Problem Statement

AI agents are becoming omnipresent but most agentic pipelines are deployed server-side, requiring users to share raw screen data — including sensitive PII — with remote servers. This creates a fundamental privacy conflict: users want intelligent assistance, but don't want their passwords, faces, financial data, and personal information leaving their device.

Modern browser APIs (WebGPU, WebAssembly) and local inference libraries (ONNX Runtime Web, Transformers.js) have unlocked the ability to run lightweight ML models directly in the browser. We can now build a **client-side privacy firewall** that bridges local privacy enforcement with cloud-based AI reasoning.

## 1.2 Product Vision

**Veilex** is a browser extension that acts as a **local privacy firewall** between the user's screen and a remote AI reasoning server. It captures the user's screen state, automatically detects and redacts all sensitive/PII data locally, sends only the sanitized visual context to a server-side VLM, and executes the returned actions on the browser DOM.

> **The local component is NOT an AI assistant — it is a privacy firewall.**  
> **The server component IS the AI assistant — but it never sees raw PII.**

## 1.3 Target Users

| User | Pain Point | How Veilex Helps |
|---|---|---|
| **Privacy-conscious users** | Don't trust cloud AI with their screens | All PII redacted before any data leaves the device |
| **Enterprise employees** | Company policy forbids sending data to external AI | Extension enforces data sanitization at the browser level |
| **Accessibility users** | Need AI help navigating complex workflows | VLM reasons about page structure and executes actions |
| **Non-technical users** | Struggle with complex multi-step web tasks | Natural language commands → automated browser actions |

## 1.4 Core User Flow

```
User visits a webpage
        │
        ▼
User presses Ctrl+Shift+V or clicks extension icon
        │
        ▼
User types: "Help me fill out this form"
        │
        ▼
Extension AUTOMATICALLY (no user action needed):
  ├── Captures screenshot + DOM
  ├── Detects all PII (faces, emails, passwords, cards, etc.)
  ├── Redacts PII on screenshot (blur/mask/black)
  ├── Replaces PII in DOM with [TYPE_REDACTED] tokens
  └── Shows privacy summary: "Redacted: 2 faces, 3 emails, 1 password"
        │
        ▼
ONLY sanitized data sent to server (HTTPS)
        │
        ▼
Server VLM reasons about page + returns actions
        │
        ▼
Extension executes actions (click, type, scroll)
        │
        ▼
Loop: re-capture → re-redact → next action
```

## 1.5 Functional Requirements

### FR-1: Screen Capture
- **FR-1.1**: Capture the visible browser tab as a screenshot (PNG → JPEG)
- **FR-1.2**: Extract a structured DOM snapshot (all interactive elements with types, labels, positions)
- **FR-1.3**: Support configurable capture resolution (default 1280×720, adaptive to hardware)
- **FR-1.4**: Rate-limit captures to max 1 per 2 seconds

### FR-2: PII Detection (Client-Side)
- **FR-2.1**: Detect form-field PII via DOM attributes (`type=password`, `autocomplete=cc-number`, etc.)
- **FR-2.2**: Detect text PII via regex (email, phone, SSN, credit card, Aadhaar, PAN, IP, DOB)
- **FR-2.3**: Detect faces via BlazeFace ML model (~400KB)
- **FR-2.4**: Detect text in images via Tesseract.js OCR (on-demand, lazy-loaded)
- **FR-2.5**: Classify sensitive document types (ID cards, medical forms) via MobileNet-v2
- **FR-2.6**: Adapt detection depth to hardware capability (3-tier system)

### FR-3: Redaction (Client-Side)
- **FR-3.1**: Apply visual redaction on screenshot canvas (blur faces, black-out text PII, pixelate documents)
- **FR-3.2**: Apply 10-15% safety margin padding around detected regions
- **FR-3.3**: Replace PII text in DOM snapshot with typed `[TYPE_REDACTED]` tokens
- **FR-3.4**: Generate a redaction manifest (what was redacted, where, by which detector, with what confidence)
- **FR-3.5**: All redaction must complete BEFORE any network request

### FR-4: Server Communication
- **FR-4.1**: Transmit sanitized context (redacted screenshot + clean DOM + manifest) via HTTPS POST
- **FR-4.2**: Compress payload via gzip (`CompressionStream` API)
- **FR-4.3**: Target payload size < 500KB per request
- **FR-4.4**: Timeout at 30 seconds with 2 retries and exponential backoff

### FR-5: Server-Side Reasoning
- **FR-5.1**: Receive sanitized context and construct multimodal VLM prompt
- **FR-5.2**: System prompt makes VLM aware of redaction scheme (never guess redacted content)
- **FR-5.3**: Return structured action commands (click, type, scroll, select, navigate, wait, read)
- **FR-5.4**: Include human-readable explanation of reasoning

### FR-6: Action Execution (Client-Side)
- **FR-6.1**: Validate server responses against strict action schema whitelist
- **FR-6.2**: Block dangerous actions (no `eval()`, no script injection, no untrusted navigations)
- **FR-6.3**: Execute actions with visual overlay feedback (user sees what's happening)
- **FR-6.4**: Support multi-step flows (execute → re-capture → next action loop)
- **FR-6.5**: Rate limit: max 10 actions per response, max 1 action per 500ms

### FR-7: User Interface
- **FR-7.1**: Popup with text prompt input and "Go" button
- **FR-7.2**: Pipeline status indicator (Capturing → Detecting → Redacting → Sending → Executing)
- **FR-7.3**: Privacy log showing redaction summary per session
- **FR-7.4**: Latency/metrics display (timing breakdown per stage)
- **FR-7.5**: Settings: sensitivity level, server URL, hardware tier display
- **FR-7.6**: Keyboard shortcut: Ctrl+Shift+V to activate

## 1.6 Non-Functional Requirements

| ID | Requirement | Target |
|---|---|---|
| **NFR-1** | Raw PII must NEVER leave the device | Zero PII in network traffic |
| **NFR-2** | Must work without local LLM/GPU | CPU/WASM fallback mandatory |
| **NFR-3** | Total bundled model size | < 10MB |
| **NFR-4** | Main thread must never block | All ML in Web Workers / OffscreenDocument |
| **NFR-5** | End-to-end latency (prompt → action) | < 5 seconds |
| **NFR-6** | Memory usage during inference | < 200MB additional |
| **NFR-7** | Works on Chrome 120+ and Firefox 115+ | Cross-browser |
| **NFR-8** | Privacy filtering must be automatic | No manual "sanitize" button |

## 1.7 Evaluation Metrics Alignment

| Metric | Weight | Our Strategy | Target |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Visual context accuracy** | 25% | Full DOM snapshot + redacted screenshot preserves page structure. `[TYPE_REDACTED]` tokens keep semantic meaning. Server VLM can still reason about layout. | > 85% task completion on test scenarios |
| **PII detection recall/precision** | 20% | 3-tier hybrid: DOM attributes (high precision), regex (high recall), vision models (faces/documents). Union of all detectors maximizes recall. | Recall > 95%, Precision > 90% |
| **Redaction precision** | 20% | Tight bounding boxes with 10-15% safety margin. Type-specific redaction (blur, black, mosaic). Tokens preserve semantics. | Zero PII leakage in output |
| **Client resource utilization** | 20% | Adaptive 3-tier system. Low-end: DOM+regex only (0 ML cost). Models < 10MB. Inference in workers. | < 200MB RAM, < 50% CPU spike |
| **E2E latency** | 15% | Tier 1 < 50ms, Tier 2 < 200ms, capture < 100ms, network < 1s, server < 3s | < 5s total pipeline |

## 1.8 Technology Stack

| Component | Technology | Size/Cost |
|---|---|---|
| Extension framework | Chrome Manifest V3 + Firefox `browser-polyfill` | — |
| DOM PII detection | Pure JavaScript (rules + regex) | 0 MB, 0 ML |
| Face detection | BlazeFace via ONNX Runtime Web | ~400KB |
| Image classification | MobileNet-v2 INT8 via ONNX Runtime Web | ~5MB |
| OCR (on-demand) | Tesseract.js (WASM) | ~2MB (lazy-loaded) |
| ML runtime | ONNX Runtime Web (WASM + WebGPU) | ~2MB |
| Screenshot redaction | HTML Canvas API | Built-in |
| Server framework | Python FastAPI + Uvicorn | — |
| Server VLM (primary) | **Groq API** (free tier, fast) | Free |
| Server VLM (fallback) | Qwen2-VL-7B via Ollama (local) or Gemini API | Variable |
| Action format | Structured JSON with whitelist validation | — |

## 1.9 Out of Scope (v1)

- Real-time video/screen recording redaction (we do per-frame snapshots)
- Custom user-trained PII models
- Mobile browser support
- Extension marketplace publishing
- End-to-end encryption of the sanitized payload (HTTPS is sufficient)

