### Component 3: Screen Capture Layer

#### [NEW] `extension/capture/screen-capture.js`
- Uses `chrome.tabs.captureVisibleTab()` to capture visible tab as PNG data URL
- Configurable capture resolution (default: 1280×720 to limit data size)
- Downscale on weak hardware (auto-detected via `navigator.hardwareConcurrency` and `navigator.deviceMemory`)
- Rate limiting: max 1 capture per 2 seconds to prevent resource exhaustion
- Returns: data URL string

#### [NEW] `extension/capture/dom-extractor.js`
- **Content script** that extracts a structured DOM snapshot:
  ```json
  {
    "url": "https://example.com/form",
    "title": "Sign Up",
    "elements": [
      {
        "tag": "input",
        "type": "password",
        "id": "passwd",
        "name": "password",
        "label": "Password",
        "autocomplete": "current-password",
        "placeholder": "Enter password",
        "bbox": {"x": 100, "y": 200, "w": 300, "h": 40},
        "visible": true,
        "value_length": 12
      }
    ],
    "landmarks": ["nav", "main", "header", "footer"],
    "visible_text_blocks": [
      {"text": "John Doe — john@email.com", "bbox": {"x": 50, "y": 100, "w": 400, "h": 20}}
    ]
  }
  ```
- Extracts: all `<input>`, `<textarea>`, `<select>` elements with types, labels, autocomplete hints, aria-labels
- Computes bounding boxes via `getBoundingClientRect()`
- Extracts visible text blocks with positions (for cross-referencing with vision)
- **NEVER** extracts actual password values — only metadata (type, length)
- Strips URL path parameters / query strings to prevent session token leakage (sends domain only)

