### Component 5: PII Detection — Tier 2 (Lightweight Vision, <5MB)

> **Runs on mid+ hardware. Catches visual PII that DOM/regex miss.**

#### [NEW] `extension/privacy/face-detector.js`
- Uses **MediaPipe BlazeFace** (~400KB ONNX model) via ONNX Runtime Web
- Backend selection: WebGPU → WebGL → WASM (automatic fallback)
- Input: captured screenshot (downscaled to 320×240 for detection)
- Output: Array of face bounding boxes with confidence scores
- Runs in **OffscreenDocument** (Chrome) or Web Worker to avoid blocking UI
- Inference time target: <100ms on WASM, <30ms on WebGPU

#### [NEW] `extension/privacy/ocr-detector.js`
- Uses **Tesseract.js** (WASM) for OCR on image-heavy regions
- **Triggered only when**:
  - Page contains `<canvas>`, `<img>`, or `<svg>` elements with significant area
  - DOM text coverage is low (suggesting text is rendered as images)
- Extracts text from image regions → feeds through regex-detector for PII matching
- Lazy-loaded: Tesseract worker initialized only when needed (~2MB download)
- Caches worker in `IndexedDB` for subsequent uses

---

### Component 6: PII Detection — Tier 3 (Enhanced, High-end Hardware)

> **Runs only on high-tier hardware. Catches document-level sensitivity.**

#### [NEW] `extension/privacy/vision-model.js`
- Loads a **quantized MobileNet-v2** or **EfficientNet-B0** (~5MB INT8 ONNX) for content classification
- Classifies image regions as: `document`, `id-card`, `medical-form`, `receipt`, `generic`
- If classified as sensitive document type → entire region is redacted with mosaic
- Uses ONNX Runtime Web with automatic backend selection (WebGPU → WASM)

