### Component 7: Hardware Capability Detection & Adaptive Processing

#### [NEW] `extension/core/hardware-profiler.js`
- Runs once on extension install, re-runs periodically
- Detects:
  ```js
  {
    cores: navigator.hardwareConcurrency,        // CPU cores
    memory: navigator.deviceMemory,              // RAM in GB
    webgpu: !!navigator.gpu,                     // WebGPU support
    webgl: !!canvas.getContext('webgl2'),         // WebGL2 support  
    gpu_vendor: getGPUInfo(),                     // GPU info via WebGL
    battery: navigator.getBattery(),              // Battery status
  }
  ```
- Assigns a **hardware tier**:
  
  | Tier | Criteria | Processing | Models Loaded |
  |------|----------|------------|---------------|
  | **High** | ≥8 cores, ≥8GB RAM, WebGPU | All 3 tiers, full resolution | BlazeFace + MobileNet + OCR |
  | **Mid** | ≥4 cores, ≥4GB RAM, WebGL | Tier 1 + Tier 2, medium resolution | BlazeFace + OCR (lazy) |
  | **Low** | <4 cores or <4GB RAM | Tier 1 only (DOM+regex), low resolution | None |

- Stores tier in `chrome.storage.local` for quick access
- User can override tier in settings

