### Component 8: Redaction Engine

> **The critical output layer. Produces the sanitized context that is safe to transmit.**

#### [NEW] `extension/redaction/visual-redactor.js`
- Takes the raw screenshot (as Canvas/ImageBitmap) + all detected PII regions
- For each PII region with a bounding box:
  - **Faces**: Gaussian blur (`ctx.filter = 'blur(20px)'`) + overlay label `[FACE]`
  - **Passwords/Cards/SSN/Aadhaar/PAN**: Solid black rectangle + overlay with redaction token text
  - **Documents/ID cards**: Heavy pixelation (mosaic) + overlay label `[DOCUMENT]`
  - **Text PII (email, phone, DOB)**: Black rectangle precisely covering the text bbox
- Applies a **safety margin** of 10-15% padding around each bbox to prevent partial leakage
- Outputs: redacted screenshot as JPEG (**quality 0.80** — balances bandwidth vs VLM readability)
- All operations use HTML Canvas API — no external dependency

#### [NEW] `extension/redaction/dom-redactor.js`
- Takes the DOM snapshot + all detected PII regions
- For each text-based PII:
  - Replaces actual text with the corresponding redaction token
  - Example: `"john.doe@gmail.com"` → `"[EMAIL_REDACTED]"`
  - Example: `"4532-1234-5678-9012"` → `"[CARD_REDACTED]"`
  - Example: `"ABCDE1234F"` → `"[PAN_REDACTED]"`
- For each input field PII:
  - Replaces value with token, preserves field metadata
  - Example: `{ type: "password", value: "[PASSWORD_REDACTED]", label: "Password" }`
- Preserves full DOM structure for server to understand page layout
- Outputs: sanitized DOM snapshot JSON

#### [NEW] `extension/redaction/manifest-generator.js`
- Generates a **redaction manifest** — a structured record of what was redacted:
  ```json
